<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voltaire returns one week after his first visit, with the catheter in place since then. The urine in the bag has gone from red to light pink, with one small clot four days ago and none since. He has had no fever, flank pain, or bladder spasm, and the catheter has drained without blockage. He stopped the diphenhydramine and the phosphate enemas; he slept poorly for two nights and now sleeps about five hours. His bowels open every one to two days on polyethylene glycol. He takes tamsulosin each evening without dizziness. He has cut his coffee to about five cups a day. The CT urography and chest CT were done two days after the first visit. He saw Dr. Bergström-Nwosu of urology this morning, who performed a flexible cystoscopy. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bleeding</td><td>Light pink urine; one small clot four days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Catheter</td><td>16 Fr indwelling catheter draining well; no fever or spasm</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Diphenhydramine and phosphate enemas stopped; tamsulosin tolerated; polyethylene glycol continued</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>CT urography and chest CT done two days after intake</td></tr><tr><td>Cystoscopy</td><td>Done by urology this morning</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

